			</tr></table><table width="100%"><tr><td width="80"><a href="tales.php" target="main"><font class=link1>[<< tales]</a></td><td></td></tr></table><p align=left><font class=s4><u>Lhranc's Tea Party</font><table width="100%"><tr height="25"><td></td></tr><tr><td>The day had started brightly England had beaten Denmark 3-0. The birds were singing in the trees and the sun was shining brightly on children playing happily in the fields.<br><br>But there was a shadow coming to the lands. And as the sun began to set and the shadows grew longer it seemed as though the land paused to draw breath and shudder as if it knew what was to come.<br><br>An adventuring company known as The Legions of Valhalla had been plundering the Plane of Growth for some hours. The servants of Lady Tunare lay everywhere in broken and bleeding heaps. But this evil band had been disappointed with the meagre loot that they had so far obtained.<br><br>As the Legions of Valhalla grew ever more restless and disatisfied with their raid a call came from one of their scouts in a distant land.<br><br>Ashaba Charmweaver one of the few members who could still alk in Tunare's grace had been called to the ancient ruins of The City of Mist deep in The Emerald Jungle. A group of fortune seekers had called her there to help deal with a number of creatures called Black Reavers. There were a number of ancient ghosts there as well. These ghosts were the trapped souls of many prominent Iksar at the time when their ancient empire had fallen. And these ghosts did not welcome ANYONE disturbing their rest.<br><br>Ashaba called to her guild for amongst these ghosts was the ghost of Lhranc. She knew that her estranged and very evil sister, Nefetari Bloodwych needed to kill this Lhranc as the final part of an epic quest. Perhaps if Ashaba was the one who brought news of Lhranc's appearance the to sisters might once more know the love of their childhood before politics and war had split the Erudite nation.<br><br>The smile that passed accross Nefetari's face when she heard this news was as terrible and frightening as it was beautiful. The wizard Leeonal and the dark priest Kuroman began to muster the Legions in what was left of Tunare's realm and elsehere. Far and wide the call to hunt was heard and in all corners of the World The Legions of Valhalla answered the call.<br><br>The sweet druidess Lilye Meadowrunner was seen everywhere as she used the secret forest paths known only to The Druids. She gathered The Legions to her and transported them to The Emerald Jungle. Perhaps she hoped they would feel and understand Tunare's bounty and repent of their sinful ways.<br><br>Leeonal led his wizard colleagues as more Legions were mustered. The Black Hearted Dark elf enchantress known simply as Visciousness Snakemistress worked her magics in The Dreadlands which was to be the mustering point before final deployment to The City of Mist.<br><br>The veteran gnome warrior and commander of armies, Bliza Blumpkin then took charge of the operation. With steel in his voice and determination in his heart he rallied the troops and brought them to the ancient ruins of Mist.<br><br>Omeganight Shadowwynd had been in Mist for some time acting as scout. He had heard that there would be biscuits at what was becoming known as "Lhranc's Tea party" He had negotiated with another band of adventurers and they had finally left the place leaving Lhranc open to the Legions of Valhalla.<br><br>The Undead guardians and ghosts of Mist were no match for The Legions. Smeene Battlesleeper of an obscure order of monks who believed that sleep and battle led to purity of mind and body led the way through the ruins. He claimed he had seen Lhranc and so like a pack of wolves they made their way through the feeble defenders of the city.<br><br>Finally they reached the prison where the evil essence of Lhranc had been imprisoned. The ranks parted and the beautiful Nefetari was ushered to the front. She stipped off her breastplate and gave to Lhranc the items that he had demandd from her. These were The Will of Innoruuk (her breastplate), the Heart of an Innocent, The Head of The Valiant and The Corrupted Ghoulbane.<br><br>As the evil Lhranc clasped these items to his ghostly chest he began to laugh and mock Nefetari and the Legions and it soon became clear that he had tricked The Bloodwitch. He had used her in order to get the items he needed to escape his prison and ressurrect himself.<br><br>As his treachery became obvious an unholy rage filled Nefetari's heart and she threw a curse at the evil Lhranc now in a body of flesh. Lhranc laughed and fell upon Nefetari in an attack of terrifying ferocity. She was barely able to feign death in time. She was then forcd to watch as Lhranc systematically destroyed The Legion.<br><br>Everyone was dead and all Nefetari had to show for her months of work was an old coin. She was filled with despair. Lhranc was too strong and she feared she would have to begin the quest all over again.<br><br>But as Kekkou of Innoruuk had survived the slaughter she began bringing the Legion back to life. And soon other clerics were also bringing the dead to life. And the Will of Valhalla could be heard. Lhranc had made it personal. The Legions of Valhalla had destroyed The Vindicator of Kael. They would NOT allow themselves to be defeated by Lhranc.<br><br>Lhranc drunk with power and the joy of once again being alive ignored the feeble rabble that was re organising around him. That was his only and last mistake.<br><br>Nefetari had been busy while her companions were ressurected and she had been given good advice. She bent down and whispred a plan to Bliza the gnome.<br><br>Bliza was a master of riposte a difficult and deadly form of combat. Other warriors knew this technique as well. The clerics organised their healing powers while the warriors prepared to blunt the fury of Lhranc's power.<br><br>Nefetari summoned a bone servant this time and sent it in to absorb Lhrancs first and deadliest touch. As the servant exploded in a shower of shards Bliza led the charge.<br><br>The Legions used all their power and focused it upon Lhranc in an unstoppable barrage. When Bliza went down The formidable Aenian stepped up to take his place. Aenian wielded the huge and legendary Tantor's Tusk and Lhranc's head swam from the heavy blows from this formidable weapon. With a mighty surge however Lhranc was able to slay Aenian. The two mightiest warriors were down and although Lhranc himself was gravely wounded, the battle hung momentarily in the balance.<br><br>As Lhranc's attention fell upon a third warrior, the cunning swarven rogue known as Boulderdash Orkforker snuck up behind the Deathknight and plunged his wickedly sharp knife into the spinal chord of Lhranc. And so it was with a lethal double strike that Lhranc fell to the ground. Dead once more.<br><br>Grinning evilly Nefetari turned to Marl Kastane and tossing Lhranc's coin to Marl coldly demanded that she be given The Sword of Paineel, Innoruuk's Curse. Marl agreed and hastily departed.<br><br>And The Legions of valhalla departed also. Feeling strong and victorious.<br><br>Only Ashaba stayed to give thanks to her God Quellious The Tranquil. The Sisters were moving closer. Perhaps her young Sister might one day repent of her evil ways and they would be close again.....<br><br></td></tr><tr height="25"><td></td></tr><tr><td align=center><img src="talesimg/296_0_EQ000021.jpeg"></td></tr><tr><td align=center>Mustering in Dreadlands</td></tr><tr height="25"><td></td></tr><tr><td align=center><img src="talesimg/296_1_EQ000022.jpeg"></td></tr><tr><td align=center>On the Bridge in CoM</td></tr><tr height="25"><td></td></tr><tr><td align=center><img src="talesimg/296_2_at home.jpg"></td></tr><tr><td align=center>I promised this if the guild survived and its appropriate for the story :)</td></tr><tr height="25"><td></td></tr><tr><td align=center>